00:25:45,861 --> 00:25:52,640
Polly Crist first you crack the egg on the grill like this

322
00:25:52,641 --> 00:25:55,480
You want to do it slowly and carefully.

323
00:25:56,320 --> 00:26:00,520
For Polly, sunny side up means the white is cooked all the way through, but not the yolk.

324
00:26:02,940 --> 00:26:06,200
Now, the trick to turning eggs over without breaking the yolks.

325
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,720
Just crack the egg as I said before.

326
00:26:10,700 --> 00:26:15,300
This time you want to kind of get them both together so it's easier to flip.

327
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,720
It's all on the wrist.

328
00:26:18,340 --> 00:26:20,160
The egg never leaves the griddle when it's flipped.

329
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:22,420
Over easy just cooks the white.

330
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:26,640
Over medium cooks the yolk just a touch.

331
00:26:26,641 --> 00:26:30,640
What I do is just lightly touch it.

332
00:26:30,641 --> 00:26:33,640
And it's cooked, but not all the way.

333
00:26:33,641 --> 00:26:36,640
It's usually just cooked around the edges like this.

334
00:26:36,641 --> 00:26:39,640
And you see that yellow right there? That's what you want.

335
00:26:39,641 --> 00:26:42,640
That's nice and pretty right there.

336
00:26:42,641 --> 00:26:47,640
The Hamburg, like most restaurants, serves only grade AA eggs.

337
00:26:47,641 --> 00:26:51,640
They stand up tall on a plate with firm yolks and thick whites.

338
00:26:51,641 --> 00:26:58,520
Grade A's are still good, but a bit less high profile.

339
00:26:58,521 --> 00:27:04,500
The thinner whites of a grade B make for a much flatter fried egg.

340
00:27:04,501 --> 00:27:06,500
And how about a poached egg?

341
00:27:06,501 --> 00:27:08,500
What's my secret?

342
00:27:08,501 --> 00:27:11,400
You want to look for the foam.

343
00:27:11,401 --> 00:27:17,180
As soon as the foam starts bubbling over the top, you need to turn down the heat.

344
00:27:17,181 --> 00:27:20,480
Now you can see the actual eggs still floating in there.

345
00:27:20,481 --> 00:27:24,800
They're not broken. Perfect. All the way cooked.

346
00:27:25,840 --> 00:27:29,900
For omelets, the bigger the cooking surface, the easier it gets.

347
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:35,400
Just toss, spread, load, and fold.

348
00:27:36,620 --> 00:27:43,380
A bodybuilder who consumes 80 raw egg whites per day is eating 320 grams of protein,

349
