four times the recommended daily allowance for a man weighing 220 pounds.

350
00:27:48,801 --> 00:27:52,740
The egg will return on Modern Marvels.

351
00:27:54,420 --> 00:27:58,040
We now return to the egg on Modern Marvels.

352
00:27:59,740 --> 00:28:02,740
This is an egg.

353
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:05,660
More specifically, an ostrich egg.

354
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:09,760
Containing 24 times the white and yolk of an average chicken egg.

355
00:28:12,460 --> 00:28:16,220
And this is ostrich farm owner Doug Osborne.

356
00:28:16,221 --> 00:28:21,040
giving his daily warnings to ravens eyeing the piles of eggs that have been laid overnight.

357
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:27,460
There go the ravens. There we go. I'll stay away for an hour or two.

358
00:28:29,340 --> 00:28:32,853
1,500 ostriches currently live on Osborne's O.K.

359
00:28:32,854 --> 00:28:36,220
Corral ostrich farm in Oro Grande, California.

360
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:42,380
He raises many for meat, which is in great demand for its flavor, tenderness, and low-fat content.

361
00:28:42,381 --> 00:28:47,340
But he is also one of the nation's most prominent producers of ostrich eggs.

362
00:28:48,220 --> 00:28:49,720
And yes, they are edible.

363
00:28:50,980 --> 00:28:54,880
One of the things we believe here on the ostrich farm is that you are what you eat.

364
00:28:55,660 --> 00:28:58,680
And if you are what you eat, the ostrich lives 100 years,

365
00:28:59,100 --> 00:29:02,200
he runs 50 miles an hour, and he mates three times a day.

366
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:03,960
I mean, what more could you ask for?

367
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:09,980
For reasons that should be obvious, the OK Corral is a cage-free farm.

368
00:29:09,981 --> 00:29:16,160
Ostriches standing as high as 9 feet tall with more devastating leg kick power than

369
00:29:16,161 --> 00:29:20,960
a horse wouldn't have it any other way.

370
00:29:20,961 --> 00:29:21,960
They don't fly.

371
00:29:21,961 --> 00:29:24,120
They don't need to.

372
00:29:24,121 --> 00:29:28,300
Like chickens, ostriches are followers when it comes to nesting.

373
00:29:28,301 --> 00:29:33,420
When one decides to lay an egg in a particular location, others literally stand in line to

374
00:29:33,421 --> 00:29:34,420
follow.

375
00:29:34,421 --> 00:29:40,040
We're out here in the southeast corner of the ostrich pen and the eggs are laid

376
00:29:40,041 --> 00:29:46,640
on a daily basis. Hens will generally lay about two eggs a week and in his pen we

377
00:29:46,641 --> 00:29:54,320
have 450 breeders of which about 300 are hens. So we get hundreds of eggs on a

378
00:29:54,321 --> 00:29:59,700
weekly basis and this is a typical nest of ostrich eggs here and they put little

379
00:29:59,701 --> 00:30:04,100
pods of dirt. They pick up dirt and sprinkle the dirt on top of the eggs and

380
00:30:04,101 --> 00:30:10,040
And I suspect that the reason for that, in Africa, this would be a good camouflage,

381
00:30:10,420 --> 00:30:12,600
maybe an odor-proofing or something,

382
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:18,160
where other animals wouldn't come along and want to eat or destroy their eggs.

383
00:30:19,700 --> 00:30:24,080
After gathering the eggs, Osborne candles them with a low-tech flashlight.

384
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:28,240
Those showing signs of fertility are placed in an incubator.

385
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:31,340
Infertile eggs are prepared for shipment.

386
00:30:31,341 --> 00:30:36,140
Ostrich eggs actually have two markets.

387
00:30:36,141 --> 00:30:41,340
The contents for eating and the shelves as collector's items or for artwork.

388
00:30:41,341 --> 00:30:43,444
Twenty miles from the O.K.

389
00:30:43,445 --> 00:30:48,220
Corral Farm sits the West Coast home of the ostrich omelet,

390
00:30:48,221 --> 00:30:51,220
the Summit Inn on historic Route 66.

391
00:30:51,221 --> 00:30:52,220
There you go.

392
00:30:52,221 --> 00:30:56,720
I want to show you the way I open the eggs.

393
00:30:56,721 --> 00:31:01,340
When an order comes in for an ostrich omelet, the first kitchen gadget chef Aureliano Rios

394
00:31:01,341 --> 00:31:07,020
chooses is a dremel, the kind of tool a mason uses to drill into concrete.

395
00:31:07,021 --> 00:31:11,620
Because the shells alone sell for $10 or more, the contents of the egg are emptied through

396
00:31:11,621 --> 00:31:13,900
a tiny hole.

397
00:31:13,901 --> 00:31:20,380
Even the most powerful stone dremel bit requires serious pressure to pierce the hard shell.

398
00:31:20,381 --> 00:31:27,480
An ostrich eggshell is so hard, a 200-pound man could stand on it, and it wouldn't break.

399
00:31:27,481 --> 00:31:31,920
So how do ostrich chicks ever make their way out?

400
00:31:31,921 --> 00:31:38,500
Over time, approximately 45 days, thousands of microscopic pores in the shell expand,

401
00:31:38,501 --> 00:31:43,280
making it breakable at just the right time for a baby ostrich to peck or kick its way

402
00:31:43,281 --> 00:31:45,780
out.

403
00:31:45,781 --> 00:31:50,080
The expansion of pores occurs with all eggs, including those laid by a chicken.

404
00:31:50,081 --> 00:31:57,320
For the ostrich egg chef, once a hole is drilled into a shell, a vacuum device empties

405
00:31:57,321 --> 00:31:59,900
out the white and the yolk.

406
00:31:59,901 --> 00:32:03,540
And the scrambled egg mix finds its way to the griddle.

407
00:32:03,541 --> 00:32:05,940
A very large griddle.

408
00:32:05,941 --> 00:32:12,920
A whole ostrich egg packs over 2,000 calories and 33 grams of protein.

409
00:32:12,921 --> 00:32:18,080
Coincidentally, the minimum daily requirement for an average healthy adult.

410
00:32:18,081 --> 00:32:19,960
The cholesterol level?

411
00:32:19,961 --> 00:32:24,060
Approximately 16 times that of a chicken egg.

412
00:32:24,061 --> 00:32:30,160
This omelet also includes cheese and ostrich meat.

413
00:32:30,161 --> 00:32:37,740
The real cooking trick comes when it's time to fold the omelet for plating.

414
00:32:37,741 --> 00:32:50,060
Voila, the only single egg omelet that won't fit on a large plate.

415
00:32:50,061 --> 00:32:53,860
Exotic eggs don't just come from unusual birds.

416
00:32:53,861 --> 00:32:59,640
Some chicken eggs fall into that category as the result of preparation.

417
00:32:59,641 --> 00:33:05,260
Any purple egg may not seem appetizing to the uninitiated, but at Philippe's restaurant

418
00:33:05,261 --> 00:33:10,440
in Los Angeles, their homemade pickled eggs are so popular, they need to make a new batch

419
00:33:10,441 --> 00:33:12,820
